{
 "about": "Hand labels for PU-4 calibration. 100 portfolio filings drawn with random.seed(2026) from the 455 in the fixtures (the 20-stock portfolio, filings 18 Sep to 17 Nov 2026), labelled from the exchange category, subject and one-line summary only, before the levels and scores were checked against them. Labelled by Claude (the coding model) under the definition below; a human pass would be the next step. Borderline calls made the same way throughout: independent-director changes, routine re-appointments, money moved into a wholly owned subsidiary, subsidiary closures and orders with no amount are not material; business-head changes under a new CEO and a regulator's decision that changes a business are.",
 "definition": "Material = a long-only fund manager who owns the stock would want to see it today: results and results decks or releases with numbers; business updates with numbers; M&A, stake sales, JVs, licensing deals; top-management or board changes (CXO, MD, deputy MD, chairman, promoter-group director); fund raises of size (QIP, large NCD programmes); regulatory approvals or actions; new orders or capacity of size. Not material: meeting schedules, transcripts and recordings, trading-window closures, ESOP allotments and grants, certificates, newspaper ads, postal ballots and AGM/EGM notices, dividend record dates, rating reaffirmations, routine re-appointments, routine debt issuance by a lender, product or client announcements without numbers.",
